   "role": "formal: the seven GL1 import lines of the estate's Lean import root \u2014 evidence that THIS edition's seven Lean sources are imported by it. WHAT IT DOES NOT ESTABLISH: that those sources are sorry-free on the clean axiom triple. That is the release log, which is its own row; this row is about imports and nothing else.",
   "slice_rule": {
    "regex": "^import Sandbox\\.A1\\.GL1(\\.|$)",
    "sort": true,
    "reproduce": "the matching lines of Sandbox.lean, sorted, joined by newline, one trailing newline, sha256 of the UTF-8 bytes",
    "why": "A whole-file hash was the wrong instrument for this row's claim and was wrong in BOTH directions: it fired on an import added for the AN tree, which has nothing to do with GL1, and it would NOT have fired if a GL1 import were removed while the file changed size elsewhere. The slice isolates the bytes the claim is about, so it fires exactly when a GL1 source leaves the import root and at no other time."
   },
   "shipped_is": "a SLICE of the source file, not the file - the lines its regex selects, sorted. The rule ships with it so a reader reproduces it from their own copy of the source.",
